mothershipOS (mship display): real present fences for the ranchu HWC. The guest virtio-gpu fences
every primary flush (guest/drivers/virtio_gpu), so the blocking commit returns once the frame is on
the host panel and its out fence's signal time is the present time. The HWC no longer reports
PRESENT_FENCE_IS_NOT_RELIABLE, and its software vsync is phase-locked (low-pass) to those present
times, so SurfaceFlinger's vsync model, hardware vsync and present fences all follow the panel
(device/google/cuttlefish 0005 turns the sync framework on).

